%description:

Known deviation: Tr36814PathLossModel has the RMa and SMa LOS-probability
decay constants swapped.

3GPP TR 36.814 v9.2.0, Table A.2.1.1.2-3, which reproduces the LOS
probabilities of ITU-R M.2135-1 Table A1-3, gives

    RMa:  P = 1                          d <= 10 m
          P = exp(-(d - 10) / 1000)      d > 10 m
    SMa:  P = 1                          d <= 10 m
          P = exp(-(d - 10) / 200)       d > 10 m

Tr36814PathLossModel::computeLosProbability() uses 200 for RMa and 1000 for
SMa, i.e. it makes the rural scenario lose line of sight five times faster
than the suburban one. At 500 m it reports 8.6% LOS in RMa and 61.3% in SMa,
where the specification asks for 61.3% and 8.6% respectively.

Tr36873PathLossModel and Tr38901PathLossModel both use 1000 for RMa, so the
three models also disagree with each other on the same link.

%expected-failure: the RMa and SMa LOS-probability decay constants are swapped

%includes:
#include "PathLossTestUtil.h"
#include "simu5g/stack/phy/channelmodel/Tr36814PathLossModel.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;

%activity:
NumericChecker c(1e-8);
Tr36814PathLossModel m;
ScenarioParams p;

p = ScenarioParams();
p.scenario = RURAL_MACROCELL;
p.apply(m, this);

c.check("814 RMa d=5",   m.computeLosProbability(5, 5),     1.0);
c.check("814 RMa d=10",  m.computeLosProbability(10, 10),   1.0);
c.check("814 RMa d=100", m.computeLosProbability(100, 100), 0.913931185);
c.check("814 RMa d=500", m.computeLosProbability(500, 500), 0.612626394);

p.scenario = SUBURBAN_MACROCELL;
p.apply(m, this);

c.check("814 SMa d=5",   m.computeLosProbability(5, 5),     1.0);
c.check("814 SMa d=10",  m.computeLosProbability(10, 10),   1.0);
c.check("814 SMa d=100", m.computeLosProbability(100, 100), 0.637628152);
c.check("814 SMa d=500", m.computeLosProbability(500, 500), 0.086293586);

c.summary();

%contains: stdout
checks=8 failures=0

%not-contains: stdout
FAILED
